[Applause]  [Music]  it's the hottest ticket in town  because it's the first ticket in town  tribeca will be the first  in-person film festival to take place in  all of north america  since the pandemic began over a year ago  it's also a key milestone  the 20th anniversary of the festival the  festival was founded shortly after the 9  11 attacks on the world trade center  to help revitalize the devastated nearby  tribeca neighborhood  as well as the rest of new york city  film critic allison wilmore says that  after covet 19 hit new york city  particularly hard last year  tribeca's original message of hope rings  truer than ever  now the festival is on its 20th  anniversary and it's  kind of in the wake of a trauma again  and in this case  you really feel that the festival is  trying to coax people back outside you  know back  out to the movies out to outdoor  screenings  and out to this kind of general activity  in a city that's slowly reopening  [Music]  the festival kicks off fittingly perhaps  within the heights  a new york set story adapted from  lin-manuel miranda's award-winning  broadway musical  other highlights include the world  premiere of steven soderbergh's  no sudden move  and roadrunner a behind the scenes film  about the life of the late new york chef  author and tv host anthony bourdain but  it's also a festival where  new filmmakers are hoping to make their  mark  like with this tv docu-series  incarceration nations  about prison systems around the world  director and writer  baz dreisinger says tribeca is a welcome  opportunity  it's amazing to be a part of any  in-person event frankly  as a as a filmmaker as an artist as an  activist  to be able to interact with audiences  again to do this in person and  it also feels like you know not only the  eyes of all of new york but the  the world and is watching june 19th will  be another highlight  because that's when the radio city music  hall will reopen for the first time  after being closed for more than a year  because of the coronavirus pandemic  it will host the closing night film of  tribeca  all of the audience will be fully  vaccinated and  masks will be optional it will be a  landmark event  not only for the festival but for this  city as a whole  gabriel zondo al jazeera new york

